sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Client
  participant JobAPI
  participant PostgreSQL
  participant Scheduler
  participant Redis
  participant Worker

  Note over Worker,Redis: RETRY path
  Worker->>PostgreSQL: claim job queued to running
  Worker->>Worker: run handler, raises retryable error
  alt attempts < max_attempts
    Worker->>PostgreSQL: set job retrying, next_attempt_at = now + backoff with jitter
    Scheduler->>PostgreSQL: retry promoter moves retrying to queued
    Scheduler->>Redis: LPUSH job_id
  else final attempt exhausted
    Worker->>PostgreSQL: set job failed and dead_lettered
    Worker->>Redis: LPUSH job_id to dead-letter list
  end

  Note over Client,Worker: CANCELLATION of a running job
  Client->>JobAPI: POST /jobs/{id}/cancel
  JobAPI->>PostgreSQL: SELECT job FOR UPDATE
  JobAPI->>PostgreSQL: set status cancelling, cancellation_requested_at
  JobAPI-->>Client: 202 accepted
  Worker->>PostgreSQL: next checkpoint reads cancellation_requested_at
  alt cancellation observed first
    Worker->>Worker: stop at a safe point
    Worker->>PostgreSQL: finalize job cancelled, insert notification_outbox row
  else job finishes first
    Worker->>PostgreSQL: finalize job succeeded, cancelling to succeeded
  end
